# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
#
# target/linux/hisilicon/luofu/config-6.18
#
# DERIVED FILE - do not edit symbol values by hand. Regenerate in an OpenWrt
# tree that has this target (target/linux/hisilicon) and the
# patches-6.18/ kernel series applied:
#
#     make kernel_oldconfig
#
# (or the equivalent "make -C target/linux oldconfig").
#
# This is the kernel-config DELTA against target/linux/generic/config-6.18,
# exactly the format OpenWrt emits (scripts/kconfig.pl merge -> kernel
# oldconfig -> scripts/kconfig.pl diff + generic/config-filter). It is not a
# full .config; symbols that already match the generic config are deliberately
# absent.
#
# Derivation run (2026-11-18, host-only, no device):
#   tree:      openwrt main, commit 27663a0, linux-6.18.60
#   patches:   target/linux/hisilicon/patches-6.18/001-002 applied by
#              "make target/linux/prepare" (RC=0)
#   toolchain: the tree's own OpenWrt GCC 14.4.0 toolchain was built by the
#              canonical top-level "make kernel_oldconfig" itself
#              (arm-openwrt-linux-muslgnueabi-gcc, OpenWrt GCC 14.4.0
#              toolchain-c0e63334e4)
#   command:   yes "" | make kernel_oldconfig        -> RC=0
#   merge:     scripts/kconfig.pl + generic/config-6.18 luofu/config-6.18
#   resolve:   kernel "make oldconfig" (the tree path; non-interactive preset)
#   emit:      scripts/kconfig.pl - ">" generic/config-6.18 .config
#              generic/config-filter   -> this file
#   verified:  a second "make kernel_oldconfig" produced a byte-identical
#              luofu/config-6.18 (CANONICAL_DERIVATION_IDEMPOTENT)
#   earlier:   a first pass with the bench Arm GNU Toolchain 11.3 (cross-
#              compiler override, before the OpenWrt toolchain existed)
#              produced this same delta except the compiler-feature symbol
#              CONFIG_GCC_ASM_GOTO_OUTPUT_BROKEN, which GCC 14.4 does not set.
#              That symbol is compiler-dependent and is deliberately absent.
#
# PROVENANCE LEGEND (see opensource/docs/SKELETON-SMOKE.md, 2026-11-18 section)
#   [P]  user-selectable symbol added before the derivation to select the 6.18
#        ARMv7 / Hisilicon / luofu platform. The lab 5.10.201 config had the
#        value; the previous 5.10-derived reference here had lost it.
#   [L]  value taken from the lab 5.10.201 reference (the only kernel the lab
#        has evidence for) and confirmed to still exist in 6.18. These are the
#        symbols a reviewer may compare against the bench kernel.
#   (unmarked) produced by 6.18 oldconfig select/default resolution - NOT a
#        design statement. They are reproducible from the command above.
#   [D-default] symbols that 6.18 turns on only because ARCH_HISI=y has
#        "default ARCH_HISI" in their Kconfig entries (Hisilicon clock/reset/
#        thermal drivers for other SoCs). Harmless for a build but they should
#        be pruned before submission (see the note below the entries).
#   [N]  new in the luofu driver series (patches-6.18/004-010):
#        the drivers and the dependencies they select. The 2026-11-18
#        canonical derivation predates these Kconfig entries, so the lines
#        were added by hand; for 004-005 a canonical re-derivation with the
#        patches applied produces the same symbol set (verified 2026-11-18:
#        the only differences are absent annotations and the emitted line
#        order). The 007-009 network drivers are plain tristates that reuse
#        symbols already in this delta (CONFIG_OF_MDIO, CONFIG_MDIO_BUS,
#        CONFIG_PHYLIB), so they add no resolved dependency line; GEMAC is
#        partial (binding/resource driver only, no data path - see its
#        Kconfig help). The 010 restart driver is a bool that selects
#        CONFIG_MFD_SYSCON, which is already in this delta, so it adds no
#        resolved dependency line either.
#
# WHAT THE 5.10 REFERENCE HAD THAT IS NOT IN THIS DELTA
#   * inherited from target/linux/generic/config-6.18 (equal value, therefore
#     not part of the delta): CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD, CONFIG_BRIDGE, CONFIG_JFFS2_FS, CONFIG_JFFS2_FS_WRITEBUFFER, CONFIG_MTD, CONFIG_MTD_BLKDEVS, CONFIG_MTD_BLOCK, CONFIG_MTD_OF_PARTS, CONFIG_NET, CONFIG_NET_SWITCHDEV, CONFIG_PINCONF, CONFIG_PRINTK, CONFIG_SERIAL_8250, CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE, CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_NR_UARTS, CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_RUNTIME_UARTS, CONFIG_SERIAL_EARLYCON, CONFIG_SQUASHFS, CONFIG_SQUASHFS_XZ, CONFIG_VLAN_8021Q, CONFIG_VMSPLIT_3G, CONFIG_WATCHDOG
#   * not a symbol in 6.18 at all (lab driver names, or renamed/removed
#     options - the drivers still have to be written):
#     CONFIG_LUOFU_WATCHDOG, CONFIG_MDIO_DEVICE, CONFIG_MDIO_DEVRES, CONFIG_MTD_NAND_LUOFU, CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NAND, CONFIG_PCI_MSI_IRQ_DOMAIN
#   * still present in 6.18 but hidden (promptless, select-only) and not
#     selected by this configuration, so they are not part of the delta:
#     CONFIG_I2C_DESIGNWARE_PLATFORM, CONFIG_MTD_NAND_CORE, CONFIG_PCIE_DW, CONFIG_PCIE_DW_HOST
#
# REMOVED/DOWNGRADED BY 6.18 RESOLUTION
#   CONFIG_PHYLINK: y -> m. PHYLINK is a hidden (promptless) tristate selected
#   by its users (here NET_DSA=m), so the 5.10 y value was not user-settable in
#   6.18; m is the resolved value.
#   CONFIG_GCC_ASM_GOTO_OUTPUT_BROKEN is not written by a GCC 14.4 derivation;
#   it is a compiler-feature symbol, not a target property.
#
# NOT PROVEN: with this config and the platform patches, the OpenWrt GCC
# 14.4.0 toolchain build reaches arch/arm/kernel/head.o and then fails on the
# non-immediate TEXT_OFFSET value of patch 002 (documented blocker 1 in
# opensource/docs/SKELETON-SMOKE.md); no kernel image was produced with a
# correct text offset and nothing here boots.

